@* AdminCategories.razor — Phase 3.3 v5 (horizontal node-tree, end-of-group + buttons)

   Staff-facing category management page at route `/Admin/Categories`.
   Reached from the sidebar's "Admin → Manage Categories" link (already
   wired in MainLayout.razor). Role-gated to Admin / Manager via
   [Authorize(Roles=...)] — Employees cannot create categories (the
   CreateCategoryCommand requires Manager or Admin role).

   v5 — End-of-group + buttons (replaces v4 per-node + buttons):
     Each node no longer carries its own "+" button. Instead, ONE "+"
     button appears at the END of each children group:
       - At the bottom of the root-level list of categories → adds a
         new top-level Category.
       - At the bottom of each Category's sub-cat list (visible only
         when that Category is expanded) → adds a new SubCategory
         under THAT specific Category.
       - At the bottom of each SubCategory's sub-sub list (visible
         only when that SubCategory is expanded) → adds a new
         SubSubCategory under THAT specific SubCategory.
     This matches the user's mental model: "all categories in one
     column, all sub-cats in another, all sub-subs in another — and
     under the LAST node of each column there's a + sign".

     Each node carries TWO action icons (on the node itself, not below):
       - Pencil (edit / rename) — always visible.
       - Activate/Deactivate toggle — shows "deactivate" (e.g. block
         icon) when the node is active, "activate" (e.g. check_circle)
         when the node is inactive. Clicking dispatches the right
         Activate/Deactivate command for the node's level.

     Deactivated nodes get a RED outline (instead of v4's opacity
     reduction) so they're immediately visible at a glance.

     All input placeholders have been removed (the user found the
     "مثلاً گوشی‌ها" / "نام جدید را وارد کنید" hints more distracting
     than helpful — the field label above the form is enough context).

   RTL (Persian) SUPPORT:
     The tree auto-mirrors in RTL because `flex-direction: row` follows
     the inline direction — in LTR items go left-to-right (parent on
     left, children on right), in RTL items go right-to-left (parent on
     right, children on left). NO [dir="rtl"] override is needed or
     wanted; adding `flex-direction: row-reverse` under [dir="rtl"]
     would DOUBLE-reverse the axis and put the parent on the wrong
     side. The SVG connector lines are drawn by JS
     (adminCategoriesTree.js) which detects `direction: rtl` on the
     canvas and mirrors the start/end coordinates — connectors go from
     parent.left → child.right in RTL. No per-locale markup duplication.

     The tree starts at the inline-start edge of the canvas (left in
     LTR, right in RTL) — no extra padding pushes it toward the middle.

   Hierarchy:
     Category  → has many SubCategories
     SubCategory → has many SubSubCategories
     SubSubCategory → leaf (no further children — no [+] button under it)
*@

@page "/Admin/Categories"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager")]

@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Localization
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@using Radzen
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Interfaces
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.CreateCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.ActivateCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.DeactivateCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.SubcategoryCommands.CreateSubCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.ActivateSubCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.DeactivateSubCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.RenameSubCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.SubSubCategoryCommands.CreateSubSubCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.SubSubCategoryCommands.ActivateSubSubCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.SubSubCategoryCommands.DeactivateSubSubCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.SubSubCategoryCommands.RenameSubSubCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Commands.RenameCategory
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Queries.GetAllCategories
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject ICurrentUserService CurrentUser
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<AdminCategories> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject ErrorDisplayService ErrorDisplay
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .admin-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: space-between;
                gap: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            /* ── Horizontal node-tree (v5) ────────────────────────────────

                           Layout:
                             .tree-canvas    — relative-positioned container that
                                               holds the SVG overlay + the nodes layer.
                                               Overflow:auto so wide trees scroll.
                                               Padding reduced to inline-start:0 so
                                               the tree starts at the very edge.
                             .nodes-layer    — the recursive tree. Each .tree-node
                                               is a flex row: [node-content] [children]
                                               Children stack vertically, centered
                                               around the parent's Y.

                           RTL (Persian):
                             LTR layout  : parent on LEFT,  children expand to the RIGHT.
                             RTL layout  : parent on RIGHT, children expand to the LEFT.
                                           Sub-subs expand further LEFT of subs.

                             We EXPLICITLY force `flex-direction: row-reverse` under
                             [dir="rtl"] for .tree-node. This is required because the
                             flexbox `row` direction's auto-reverse behavior depends
                             on the computed `direction` of the flex container, and
                             some ancestor CSS (Radzen card/stack) interferes with
                             the inherited direction in ways that prevent the
                             spec-compliant auto-reverse. The explicit override is
                             direction-deterministic and works regardless of what
                             ancestor CSS does.

                             We also explicitly set `align-items: flex-end` on
                             .nodes-layer under [dir="rtl"] so the root categories
                             align to the RIGHT edge of the canvas (mirroring LTR's
                             `align-items: flex-start` which puts them on the LEFT). */

            .tree-canvas {
                position: relative;
                overflow: auto;
                /* inline-start padding = 0 so the root node starts at the
                               very edge of the canvas (left in LTR, right in RTL).
                               Keep some block padding so nodes don't touch the top
                               or bottom of the card. */
                padding-block: 1.5rem 2rem;
                padding-inline: 0.25rem 1rem;
                min-height: 200px;
            }

            .connectors-svg {
                position: absolute;
                inset: 0;
                width: 100%;
                height: 100%;
                pointer-events: none;
                z-index: 0;
                overflow: visible;
            }

                .connectors-svg .connector-line {
                    fill: none;
                    /* v6.2: connectors use the sub-cat icon color
                       (lighter green = --rz-success) so the lines visually
                       belong to the sub-cat level they connect, creating a
                       coherent green thread through the tree. Same color is
                       used for the list view's trunk + elbow lines. */
                    stroke: var(--rz-success, #16a34a);
                    stroke-width: 1.6;
                    stroke-linecap: round;
                }

            .nodes-layer {
                position: relative;
                z-index: 1;
                display: inline-flex; /* shrink-to-fit so canvas can scroll */
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1rem;
                /* Pull the layer to the inline-start edge so the root
                               node touches the edge (no extra indentation). */
                align-items: flex-start;
            }

            .tree-node {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: row;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 3rem; /* space between parent and its children */
            }

            /* RTL NOTE — DO NOT add a [dir="rtl"] .tree-node
                               { flex-direction: row-reverse } override here.

                               `flex-direction: row` makes the main axis follow the
                               inline direction. In LTR that is left-to-right (parent
                               on left, children on right). In RTL the browser
                               ALREADY reverses the inline direction to right-to-left
                               (parent on right, children on left) — that is exactly
                               what we want for a Persian tree.

                               Adding `row-reverse` under [dir="rtl"] DOUBLE-reverses
                               the axis: row-reverse + RTL = left-to-right physical
                               layout, which puts the parent on the LEFT of its
                               children. That was the v6 bug — "categories go to the
                               left side of the sub cats when expanded (on right to
                               left)". The fix is simply to NOT override. */

            /* ── Node content (oval + actions) ──
                           v5: actions live INSIDE the oval (right edge), not below.
                           This keeps each node compact and lets the + button sit
                           cleanly at the end of the children list. */

            .node-content {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.375rem;
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

            .node-oval {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
                min-width: 120px;
                max-width: 280px;
                border-radius: 999px; /* fully rounded = oval/pill */
                border: 1.5px solid var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18));
                background-color: var(--rz-base-background-color, #fff);
                color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                font-weight: 600;
                font-size: 0.9375rem;
                transition: border-color 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
                position: relative;
            }

                .node-oval:hover {
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary, #4338ca);
                    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(67, 56, 202, 0.12));
                }

                /* Deactivated nodes get a RED outline (replaces v4's
                               opacity reduction). Red is universally read as
                               "disabled / problematic" so the user can spot
                               deactivated nodes at a glance. */
                .node-oval.is-inactive {
                    border-color: var(--rz-danger, #dc2626);
                    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.12);
                }

                .node-oval .node-icon {
                    font-size: 1rem;
                    flex-shrink: 0;
                }

            /* ── Expand/collapse chevron ──
                               v5 originally had NO expand control on the nodes —
                               sub-cats were rendered only when isExpanded was true,
                               but nothing toggled isExpanded, so users saw "just
                               categories, nothing else". The chevron is the
                               conventional file-explorer control: click to
                               toggle the children container.

                               Placement: inline-start edge of the oval (before the
                               folder icon). Rotates based on expand state AND
                               direction (RTL flips the collapsed arrow). */
            .chevron-btn {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                width: 1.25rem;
                height: 1.25rem;
                border: none;
                background: transparent;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                cursor: pointer;
                padding: 0;
                border-radius: 4px;
                transition: background-color 0.15s ease;
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

                .chevron-btn:hover {
                    background-color: var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(67, 56, 202, 0.12));
                    color: var(--rz-primary, #4338ca);
                }

                .chevron-btn .material-icons,
                .chevron-btn .rzi {
                    font-size: 1.125rem;
                    /* Collapsed LTR: rotate -90deg → arrow points
                                       right (▶). Expanded: rotate 0 → arrow points
                                       down (▼). RTL flips the collapsed direction
                                       via the [dir="rtl"] rule below.
                                       Transition is on the icon (not the button)
                                       because the transform is applied here. */
                    transform: rotate(-90deg);
                    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
                }

                .chevron-btn.is-expanded .material-icons,
                .chevron-btn.is-expanded .rzi {
                    transform: rotate(0deg);
                }

            /* RTL: collapsed chevron points LEFT instead of
                                   right. Expanded state is the same (down) in both
                                   directions, so we don't override is-expanded. */
            [dir="rtl"] .chevron-btn:not(.is-expanded) .material-icons,
            [dir="rtl"] .chevron-btn:not(.is-expanded) .rzi {
                transform: rotate(90deg);
            }

            .node-oval .node-label {
                white-space: nowrap;
                overflow: hidden;
                text-overflow: ellipsis;
                max-width: 180px;
            }

            /* In-node action icons (right edge of the oval). They
                               appear inside the pill so they're always visible and
                               don't take up vertical space below the node. */
            .node-oval .node-actions {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.125rem;
                /* Inline-start margin pushes actions to the right
                                   edge of the oval in LTR; in RTL it flips via
                                   logical property. */
                margin-inline-start: 0.25rem;
                padding-inline-start: 0.25rem;
                border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12));
            }

            /* Inline rename form — replaces the oval's content with a
                           textbox. Keeps the oval shape so the tree layout doesn't
                           shift during editing. */
            .node-oval.is-editing {
                padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
                border-color: var(--rz-primary, #4338ca);
                box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(67, 56, 202, 0.12));
            }

                .node-oval.is-editing .rename-input {
                    border: none;
                    outline: none;
                    background: transparent;
                    font: inherit;
                    font-weight: 600;
                    color: inherit;
                    min-width: 120px;
                    max-width: 220px;
                    text-align: center;
                }

            .action-btn {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                width: 1.5rem;
                height: 1.5rem;
                border-radius: 999px;
                border: none;
                background-color: transparent;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                cursor: pointer;
                transition: all 0.15s ease;
                padding: 0;
            }

                .action-btn:hover {
                    color: var(--rz-primary, #4338ca);
                    background-color: var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(67, 56, 202, 0.12));
                }

                /* Activate/Deactivate icon — red tint when it will
                               DEACTIVATE (active node), green tint when it will
                               ACTIVATE (inactive node). Gives the user a visual
                               hint of what clicking will do. */
                .action-btn.action-toggle-will-deactivate:hover {
                    color: var(--rz-danger, #dc2626);
                    background-color: rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.12);
                }

                .action-btn.action-toggle-will-activate:hover {
                    color: var(--rz-success, #16a34a);
                    background-color: rgba(22, 163, 74, 0.12);
                }

                .action-btn .material-icons,
                .action-btn .rzi {
                    font-size: 0.9375rem;
                }

            /* ── End-of-group + button ──
                           Appears at the END of each children list (and at the end
                           of the root-level list). Clicking opens an inline add form
                           in the same spot.

                           v6.1: The + button now has a small text label BELOW it
                           explaining what clicking it will add ("Add a new category",
                           "Add sub-category", "Add sub-sub-category"). The label is
                           muted and tiny so it doesn't compete with the node names
                           for attention, but it's visible enough that a new admin
                           doesn't have to guess what the + does at each level. */

            .group-add-row {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                /* Match the .tree-node gap so the + sits in the same
                               column as the nodes above it. */
                width: 100%;
                padding-block: 0.25rem;
            }

            .group-add-btn {
                display: inline-flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                gap: 0.2rem;
                border: none;
                background-color: transparent;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                cursor: pointer;
                transition: color 0.15s ease;
                padding: 0;
                /* No fixed width/height — the icon circle + label below
                               define the size. This lets the label wrap naturally
                               if the locale's translation is long. */
            }

                .group-add-btn .add-icon-circle {
                    display: inline-flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    justify-content: center;
                    width: 2rem;
                    height: 2rem;
                    border-radius: 999px;
                    border: 1.5px dashed var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22));
                    background-color: transparent;
                    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background-color 0.15s ease, border-style 0.15s ease;
                }

                .group-add-btn:hover {
                    color: var(--rz-success, #16a34a);
                }

                    .group-add-btn:hover .add-icon-circle {
                        border-color: var(--rz-success, #16a34a);
                        background-color: rgba(22, 163, 74, 0.08);
                        border-style: solid;
                    }

                .group-add-btn .add-icon-circle .material-icons,
                .group-add-btn .add-icon-circle .rzi {
                    font-size: 1.125rem;
                }

                .group-add-btn .add-label {
                    font-size: 0.6875rem;
                    font-weight: 500;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    line-height: 1.2;
                    max-width: 120px;
                    text-align: center;
                    /* Prevent the label from making the column wider
                                   than the + icon above it — wrap to a second line
                                   instead. */
                    word-break: break-word;
                }

            /* Inline add form (replaces the + button when clicked). */
            .inline-add-form,
            .inline-rename-actions {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.25rem;
                flex-wrap: nowrap;
            }

                .inline-add-form .name-input {
                    border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18));
                    border-radius: 999px;
                    padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem;
                    font-size: 0.875rem;
                    min-width: 160px;
                    max-width: 220px;
                    outline: none;
                    background-color: var(--rz-base-background-color, #fff);
                    color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                }

                    .inline-add-form .name-input:focus {
                        border-color: var(--rz-primary, #4338ca);
                        box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(67, 56, 202, 0.12));
                    }

            /* ── Children container ── */

            .tree-children {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                justify-content: center; /* vertically center around parent */
                align-items: flex-start;
            }

            /* ── Top-level create form ──
                           v5: hidden by default. The + button at the bottom of the
                           categories list opens this form inline. The standalone
                           "create new category" card above the tree is removed —
                           adding is now done via the + button, consistent with
                           sub-cat and sub-sub-cat creation. */

            .create-form {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                align-items: center;
                flex-wrap: nowrap;
            }
            /* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
               LIST VIEW (v6 — alternative to the horizontal node-tree)
               ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
               The tree view (above) lays nodes out horizontally with SVG
               bezier connectors. Some users prefer the classic file-explorer
               "indented list with elbow connectors" layout — categories as
               top-level rows, sub-cats indented under their parent with a
               vertical line + horizontal elbow showing the parent-child
               relationship, sub-subs indented one more level.

               This CSS is COMPLETELY INDEPENDENT from the tree CSS — it uses
               different class names (.list-view, .list-row, .list-children,
               .list-node-label) so it can coexist without affecting the tree.

               Indentation + elbow connectors are drawn with pure CSS using
               logical properties (so the same rules work in both LTR and
               RTL — the vertical line appears on the inline-start edge,
               which is LEFT in English and RIGHT in Persian).

               The + buttons, edit/activate actions, and expand/collapse
               chevrons REUSE the same .action-btn / .chevron-btn / .group-add-btn
               classes from the tree view, so they look consistent across
               both views. */

            .list-view {
                /* Same canvas treatment as .tree-canvas so the two views
                   feel like the same "card". */
                padding-block: 1rem 1.5rem;
                padding-inline: 1rem;
                min-height: 200px;
            }

                .list-view .list-root {
                    display: flex;
                    flex-direction: column;
                    gap: 0.25rem;
                }

            /* A single row in the list view. Contains:
               [chevron?] [icon] [label] [actions]
               Children render BELOW (indented) inside .list-children. */
            .list-row {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                padding-block: 0.25rem;
                padding-inline: 0.5rem;
                border-radius: 6px;
                transition: background-color 0.12s ease;
            }

                .list-row:hover {
                    background-color: var(--rz-hover-background-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04));
                }

            /* The row's label — a softer, less prominent shape than the
               tree's .node-oval. List view is denser so we don't want
               every row enclosed in a heavy bordered pill. Instead the
               label sits inline with just the icon + actions. */
            .list-node-label {
                font-weight: 600;
                font-size: 0.9375rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                white-space: nowrap;
                overflow: hidden;
                text-overflow: ellipsis;
                max-width: 280px;
            }

            /* Inactive rows get a red text color + red icon (instead of
               the tree's red border, since there's no pill border here). */
            .list-row.is-inactive .list-node-label {
                color: var(--rz-danger, #dc2626);
            }

            .list-row.is-inactive .node-icon {
                color: var(--rz-danger, #dc2626) !important;
            }

            /* The inline rename textbox replaces the label. */
            .list-row .rename-input {
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-primary, #4338ca);
                border-radius: 4px;
                padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
                font: inherit;
                font-weight: 600;
                color: var(--rz-text-primary-color);
                background-color: var(--rz-base-background-color, #fff);
                min-width: 160px;
                max-width: 240px;
                outline: none;
            }

                .list-row .rename-input:focus {
                    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(67, 56, 202, 0.12));
                }

            /* Row action icons — reuse .action-btn from the tree CSS.
               The actions sit on the inline-end edge of the row. */
            .list-row .row-actions {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.125rem;
                margin-inline-start: auto; /* push to inline-end edge */
            }

            /* ── Children container with elbow connectors ──
               This is the key visual difference from the tree view.
               Each .list-children is indented on the inline-start side
               AND has a vertical line on that side, drawn via
               border-inline-start. A horizontal elbow is drawn on each
               child row via ::before pseudo-element. */
            .list-children {
                /* Indent children relative to their parent. Use logical
                   property so RTL automatically flips to the right side. */
                margin-inline-start: 1.25rem;
                /* The vertical "trunk" line — runs down the inline-start
                   edge of the children container, visually connecting all
                   siblings to their parent. */
                /* v6.2: trunk line uses the sub-cat icon color (lighter
                   green = --rz-success), matching the tree view's SVG
                   connector lines and the sub-cat circle icons. */
                border-inline-start: 1.5px solid var(--rz-success, #16a34a);
                /* Small gap so the line doesn't touch the parent row. */
                margin-block-start: 0.15rem;
                padding-inline-start: 0.5rem;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 0.15rem;
            }

            /* Horizontal elbow connector on each child row.
               The ::before pseudo-element is positioned on the inline-start
               edge (where the vertical trunk line lives) and extends
               horizontally toward the row content, creating the classic
               file-explorer "elbow" shape.

               Width is 0.5rem (matches .list-children padding-inline-start)
               so the elbow reaches from the trunk line to where the row
               content begins. */
            .list-children > .list-row::before,
            .list-children > .list-add-row::before {
                content: '';
                position: relative;
                display: block;
                width: 0.5rem;
                height: 1.5px;
                /* v6.2: elbow color matches the trunk line + tree
                   connectors (sub-cat lighter green). */
                background-color: var(--rz-success, #16a34a);
                /* Pull it back so it visually connects to the parent's
                   vertical trunk line (which lives in the parent
                   .list-children's border-inline-start). */
                margin-inline-start: -1rem;
                margin-inline-end: -0.25rem;
                flex-shrink: 0;
            }

            /* End-of-group + button in list view — reuse .group-add-btn
               but make it sit nicely inside the indented list. The row
               wrapper has padding so the + button aligns with the
               sibling rows above it. */
            .list-add-row {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                padding-block: 0.15rem;
                padding-inline: 0.5rem;
            }

                .list-add-row .inline-add-form .name-input {
                    min-width: 180px;
                }

            /* ── View switcher ──
               A small segmented toggle in the page header. Two buttons
               (Tree / List) — the active one is filled, the inactive one
               is outlined. */
            .view-switcher {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.25rem;
                padding: 0.2rem;
                border-radius: 8px;
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-color, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15));
                background-color: var(--rz-base-background-color, #fff);
            }

                .view-switcher .vs-btn {
                    display: inline-flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    gap: 0.3rem;
                    padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
                    border: none;
                    border-radius: 6px;
                    background-color: transparent;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    font-size: 0.8125rem;
                    font-weight: 600;
                    cursor: pointer;
                    transition: all 0.15s ease;
                }

                    .view-switcher .vs-btn:hover {
                        color: var(--rz-primary, #4338ca);
                        background-color: var(--rz-primary-lighter, rgba(67, 56, 202, 0.08));
                    }

                    .view-switcher .vs-btn.is-active {
                        color: #fff;
                        background-color: var(--rz-primary, #4338ca);
                    }

                    .view-switcher .vs-btn .material-icons,
                    .view-switcher .vs-btn .rzi {
                        font-size: 1rem;
                    }

            /* ── RTL: list view auto-mirrors ──
               Because we use logical properties (margin-inline-start,
               border-inline-start, padding-inline-start) throughout the
               list view CSS, RTL automatically mirrors the indentation
               and elbow connectors — vertical trunk line appears on the
               RIGHT in Persian, children indent to the RIGHT, elbows
               point LEFT. No [dir="rtl"] overrides needed. */
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <div class="admin-header">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="category" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
        </RadzenStack>

        @* ── View switcher (Tree ↔ List) ──
           v6: Two ways to view the same category data. Tree view is
           the horizontal node-tree with SVG bezier connectors. List
           view is the classic file-explorer layout with vertical
           indentation + elbow connectors — this is the DEFAULT view
           (v6.1). Both share the same state (expand/collapse, rename,
           activate, add) so switching mid-task works seamlessly — e.g.
           you can expand a category in tree view, switch to list view,
           and it will still be expanded. *@
        <div class="view-switcher" role="group" aria-label="@Loc["ViewModeLabel"]">
            <button type="button"
                    class="vs-btn @(_viewMode == ViewMode.Tree ? "is-active" : "")"
                    title="@Loc["ViewModeTree"]"
                    aria-pressed="@(_viewMode == ViewMode.Tree)"
                    @onclick="@(() => SetViewMode(ViewMode.Tree))">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="account_tree" />
                <span>@Loc["ViewModeTree"]</span>
            </button>
            <button type="button"
                    class="vs-btn @(_viewMode == ViewMode.List ? "is-active" : "")"
                    title="@Loc["ViewModeList"]"
                    aria-pressed="@(_viewMode == ViewMode.List)"
                    @onclick="@(() => SetViewMode(ViewMode.List))">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="list" />
                <span>@Loc["ViewModeList"]</span>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                     Style="height: 40vh;" Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                       Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                       Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Large" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["LoadingText"]"
                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
        </RadzenStack>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadCategoriesAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Empty state ──
       v5: When there are no categories at all, show a friendly empty
       state with a single + button to create the first category. No
       separate "create form" card — the + button does it inline. *@
    else if (_categories.Count == 0)
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 3rem; text-align: center;">
            <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="category" Style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyMessage"]"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); max-width: 420px;" />
                @if (_addingTopLevel)
                {
                    <div class="inline-add-form" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                        <input class="name-input"
                               value="@_newCategoryName"
                               @oninput="@(e => _newCategoryName = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                               @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleCreateCategoryAsync(); })"
                               @ref="_topLevelInputRef" />
                        <button type="button"
                                class="action-btn"
                                title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                disabled="@_isCreating"
                                @onclick="@HandleCreateCategoryAsync">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                        </button>
                        <button type="button"
                                class="action-btn"
                                title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                disabled="@_isCreating"
                                @onclick="@CancelAddTopLevel">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                        </button>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["AddFirstCategoryButton"]"
                                  Icon="add"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                  Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                  Click="@StartAddTopLevel" />
                }
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Horizontal node-tree ── *@
    else if (_viewMode == ViewMode.Tree)
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 0.5rem;">
            <div class="tree-canvas" @ref="_canvasRef">
                @* SVG overlay — connector paths are populated by JS
                   interop after every render. The <path> elements are
                   keyed by "{parentId}->{childId}" so Blazor diffs them
                   efficiently instead of recreating the whole SVG on
                   every state change. *@
                <svg class="connectors-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                    @foreach (var c in _connectors)
                    {
                        <path class="connector-line" d="@c.Path" data-from="@c.ParentId" data-to="@c.ChildId" />
                    }
                </svg>

                <div class="nodes-layer">
                    @foreach (var category in _categories)
                    {
                        @RenderCategoryNode(category)
                    }

                    @* End-of-group + button for the root level (adds a
                       new top-level Category). Replaced by an inline
                       add form when active. *@
                    <div class="group-add-row">
                        @if (_addingTopLevel)
                        {
                            <div class="inline-add-form">
                                <input class="name-input"
                                       value="@_newCategoryName"
                                       @oninput="@(e => _newCategoryName = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                                       @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleCreateCategoryAsync(); })"
                                       @ref="_topLevelInputRef" />
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="action-btn"
                                        title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                        disabled="@_isCreating"
                                        @onclick="@HandleCreateCategoryAsync">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                                </button>
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="action-btn"
                                        title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                        disabled="@_isCreating"
                                        @onclick="@CancelAddTopLevel">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                                </button>
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="group-add-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["AddCategoryButton"]"
                                    aria-label="@Loc["AddCategoryButton"]"
                                    disabled="@_isCreating"
                                    @onclick="@StartAddTopLevel">
                                <span class="add-icon-circle">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="add" />
                                </span>
                                <span class="add-label">@Loc["AddCategoryButton"]</span>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </RadzenCard>
    }
    else
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 0.5rem;">
            <div class="list-view">
                <div class="list-root">
                    @foreach (var category in _categories)
                    {
                        @RenderCategoryListItem(category)
                    }

                    @* End-of-group + button for the root level (adds a
                       new top-level Category). Same handler as the tree
                       view's + button — both views share state. *@
                    <div class="list-add-row">
                        @if (_addingTopLevel)
                        {
                            <div class="inline-add-form">
                                <input class="name-input"
                                       value="@_newCategoryName"
                                       @oninput="@(e => _newCategoryName = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                                       @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleCreateCategoryAsync(); })"
                                       @ref="_topLevelInputRef" />
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="action-btn"
                                        title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                        disabled="@_isCreating"
                                        @onclick="@HandleCreateCategoryAsync">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                                </button>
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="action-btn"
                                        title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                        disabled="@_isCreating"
                                        @onclick="@CancelAddTopLevel">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                                </button>
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="group-add-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["AddCategoryButton"]"
                                    aria-label="@Loc["AddCategoryButton"]"
                                    disabled="@_isCreating"
                                    @onclick="@StartAddTopLevel">
                                <span class="add-icon-circle">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="add" />
                                </span>
                                <span class="add-label">@Loc["AddCategoryButton"]</span>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </RadzenCard>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@* ── Recursive node renderers ────────────────────────────────────────
   Each level has its own render fragment so the markup stays readable
   and so we can pass the right depth/parent IDs down without juggling
   a tuple. The data-node-id / data-parent-id attributes are read by
   adminCategoriesTree.js to know which DOM elements to measure.

   v5: Each oval contains the node icon + label + an inline action
   group (edit + activate/deactivate). The action group is on the
   inline-end edge of the oval so it doesn't crowd the label. *@

@code {

    // ── Recursive node render: Category (depth 0) ──
    private RenderFragment RenderCategoryNode(CategoryDto category) => __builder =>
    {
        var nodeId = "cat:" + category.Id.ToString();
        var isRenaming = _renamingNode == nodeId;
        var isAddingSub = _addingSubTo == category.Id;
        var isExpanded = _expandedCategories.Contains(category.Id) || isAddingSub;

        <div class="tree-node" data-node-id="@nodeId">
            <div class="node-content">
                @if (isRenaming)
                {
                    <div class="node-oval is-editing">
                        <input class="rename-input"
                               value="@_renameValue"
                               @oninput="@(e => _renameValue = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                               @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleRenameCategoryAsync(category.Id); })"
                               @ref="_renameInputRef" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="inline-rename-actions">
                        <button type="button"
                                class="action-btn"
                                title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                disabled="@(_isRenaming && _renamingNode == nodeId)"
                                @onclick="@(() => HandleRenameCategoryAsync(category.Id))">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                        </button>
                        <button type="button"
                                class="action-btn"
                                title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                disabled="@(_isRenaming && _renamingNode == nodeId)"
                                @onclick="@CancelRename">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                        </button>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="node-oval @(category.IsActive ? "" : "is-inactive")">
                        @* Expand/collapse chevron — only for non-leaf
                           nodes (Category has SubCategories). Clicking
                           toggles _expandedCategories, which controls
                           whether the .tree-children container renders.
                           v5 originally had no chevron, so users could
                           never see sub-cats — that was the "categories
                           shown but nothing else" bug. *@
                        <button type="button"
                                class="chevron-btn @(isExpanded ? "is-expanded" : "")"
                                title="@(isExpanded ? Loc["Collapse"] : Loc["Expand"])"
                                aria-label="@(isExpanded ? Loc["Collapse"] : Loc["Expand"])"
                                aria-expanded="@isExpanded"
                                disabled="@_isRenaming"
                                @onclick="@(() => ToggleExpandCategory(category.Id))">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="expand_more" />
                        </button>
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="folder" Class="node-icon" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                        <span class="node-label">@category.Name</span>
                        <span class="node-actions">
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="action-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["EditButton"]"
                                    aria-label="@Loc["EditButton"]"
                                    disabled="@_isRenaming"
                                    @onclick="@(() => StartRenameCategory(category))">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="edit" />
                            </button>
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="action-btn @(category.IsActive ? "action-toggle-will-deactivate" : "action-toggle-will-activate")"
                                    title="@(category.IsActive ? Loc["DeactivateButton"] : Loc["ActivateButton"])"
                                    aria-label="@(category.IsActive ? Loc["DeactivateButton"] : Loc["ActivateButton"])"
                                    disabled="@_isToggling"
                                    @onclick="@(() => HandleToggleCategoryActiveAsync(category))">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="@(category.IsActive ? "block" : "check_circle")" />
                            </button>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                }

                @* Inline add form — appears under the last sub-cat of
                   this category (in the .tree-children container below)
                   when the user clicks the end-of-group + button. The
                   form itself is rendered inside the children container
                   so it sits in the same column as the sub-cats. *@
            </div>

            @* Children — render when expanded. The end-of-group +
               button (or inline add form) sits at the BOTTOM of this
               list, in the same column as the sub-cats. *@
            @if (isExpanded)
            {
                <div class="tree-children">
                    @foreach (var sub in category.SubCategories)
                    {
                        @RenderSubNode(category.Id, sub)
                    }

                    @* End-of-group + button for this Category's sub-cats
                       (adds a new SubCategory under THIS Category). *@
                    <div class="group-add-row">
                        @if (isAddingSub)
                        {
                            <div class="inline-add-form">
                                <input class="name-input"
                                       value="@_newSubName"
                                       @oninput="@(e => _newSubName = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                                       @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleCreateSubAsync(category.Id); })"
                                       @ref="_subInputRef" />
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="action-btn"
                                        title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                        disabled="@(_isCreating && _creatingFor == $"sub:{category.Id}")"
                                        @onclick="@(() => HandleCreateSubAsync(category.Id))">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                                </button>
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="action-btn"
                                        title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                        disabled="@(_isCreating && _creatingFor == $"sub:{category.Id}")"
                                        @onclick="@CancelAddSub">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                                </button>
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="group-add-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["AddSubCategoryButton"]"
                                    aria-label="@Loc["AddSubCategoryButton"]"
                                    disabled="@_isCreating"
                                    @onclick="@(() => StartAddSub(category.Id))">
                                <span class="add-icon-circle">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="add" />
                                </span>
                                <span class="add-label">@Loc["AddSubCategoryButton"]</span>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    };

    // ── Recursive node render: SubCategory (depth 1) ──
    private RenderFragment RenderSubNode(Guid categoryId, SubCategoryDto sub) => __builder =>
    {
        var nodeId = "sub:" + sub.Id.ToString();
        var parentId = "cat:" + categoryId.ToString();
        var isRenaming = _renamingNode == nodeId;
        var isAddingSubSub = _addingSubSubTo == sub.Id;
        var isExpanded = _expandedSubs.Contains(sub.Id) || isAddingSubSub;

        <div class="tree-node" data-node-id="@nodeId" data-parent-id="@parentId">
            <div class="node-content">
                @if (isRenaming)
                {
                    <div class="node-oval is-editing">
                        <input class="rename-input"
                               value="@_renameValue"
                               @oninput="@(e => _renameValue = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                               @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleRenameSubAsync(categoryId, sub.Id); })"
                               @ref="_renameInputRef" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="inline-rename-actions">
                        <button type="button"
                                class="action-btn"
                                title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                disabled="@(_isRenaming && _renamingNode == nodeId)"
                                @onclick="@(() => HandleRenameSubAsync(categoryId, sub.Id))">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                        </button>
                        <button type="button"
                                class="action-btn"
                                title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                disabled="@(_isRenaming && _renamingNode == nodeId)"
                                @onclick="@CancelRename">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                        </button>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="node-oval @(sub.IsActive ? "" : "is-inactive")">
                        @* Expand/collapse chevron for SubCategory —
                           same rationale as Category. SubSubCategory is
                           a leaf so it gets no chevron. *@
                        <button type="button"
                                class="chevron-btn @(isExpanded ? "is-expanded" : "")"
                                title="@(isExpanded ? Loc["Collapse"] : Loc["Expand"])"
                                aria-label="@(isExpanded ? Loc["Collapse"] : Loc["Expand"])"
                                aria-expanded="@isExpanded"
                                disabled="@_isRenaming"
                                @onclick="@(() => ToggleExpandSub(sub.Id))">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="expand_more" />
                        </button>
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="circle" Class="node-icon" Style="color: var(--rz-success); font-size: 0.75rem;" />
                        <span class="node-label">@sub.Name</span>
                        <span class="node-actions">
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="action-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["EditButton"]"
                                    aria-label="@Loc["EditButton"]"
                                    disabled="@_isRenaming"
                                    @onclick="@(() => StartRenameSub(categoryId, sub))">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="edit" />
                            </button>
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="action-btn @(sub.IsActive ? "action-toggle-will-deactivate" : "action-toggle-will-activate")"
                                    title="@(sub.IsActive ? Loc["DeactivateButton"] : Loc["ActivateButton"])"
                                    aria-label="@(sub.IsActive ? Loc["DeactivateButton"] : Loc["ActivateButton"])"
                                    disabled="@_isToggling"
                                    @onclick="@(() => HandleToggleSubActiveAsync(categoryId, sub))">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="@(sub.IsActive ? "block" : "check_circle")" />
                            </button>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                }
            </div>

            @if (isExpanded)
            {
                <div class="tree-children">
                    @foreach (var ssub in sub.SubSubCategories)
                    {
                        @RenderSubSubNode(categoryId, sub.Id, ssub)
                    }

                    @* End-of-group + button for this SubCategory's
                       sub-subs (adds a new SubSubCategory under THIS
                       SubCategory). *@
                    <div class="group-add-row">
                        @if (isAddingSubSub)
                        {
                            <div class="inline-add-form">
                                <input class="name-input"
                                       value="@_newSubSubName"
                                       @oninput="@(e => _newSubSubName = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                                       @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleCreateSubSubAsync(categoryId, sub.Id); })"
                                       @ref="_subSubInputRef" />
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="action-btn"
                                        title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                        disabled="@(_isCreating && _creatingFor == $"subsub:{sub.Id}")"
                                        @onclick="@(() => HandleCreateSubSubAsync(categoryId, sub.Id))">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                                </button>
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="action-btn"
                                        title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                        disabled="@(_isCreating && _creatingFor == $"subsub:{sub.Id}")"
                                        @onclick="@CancelAddSubSub">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                                </button>
                            </div>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="group-add-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["AddSubSubCategoryButton"]"
                                    aria-label="@Loc["AddSubSubCategoryButton"]"
                                    disabled="@_isCreating"
                                    @onclick="@(() => StartAddSubSub(sub.Id))">
                                <span class="add-icon-circle">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="add" />
                                </span>
                                <span class="add-label">@Loc["AddSubSubCategoryButton"]</span>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
        </div>
    };

    // ── Recursive node render: SubSubCategory (depth 2 — leaf) ──
    private RenderFragment RenderSubSubNode(Guid categoryId, Guid subId, SubSubCategoryDto ssub) => __builder =>
    {
        var nodeId = "subsub:" + ssub.Id.ToString();
        var parentId = "sub:" + subId.ToString();
        var isRenaming = _renamingNode == nodeId;

        <div class="tree-node" data-node-id="@nodeId" data-parent-id="@parentId">
            <div class="node-content">
                @if (isRenaming)
                {
                    <div class="node-oval is-editing">
                        <input class="rename-input"
                               value="@_renameValue"
                               @oninput="@(e => _renameValue = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                               @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleRenameSubSubAsync(categoryId, subId, ssub.Id); })"
                               @ref="_renameInputRef" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="inline-rename-actions">
                        <button type="button"
                                class="action-btn"
                                title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                disabled="@(_isRenaming && _renamingNode == nodeId)"
                                @onclick="@(() => HandleRenameSubSubAsync(categoryId, subId, ssub.Id))">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                        </button>
                        <button type="button"
                                class="action-btn"
                                title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                disabled="@(_isRenaming && _renamingNode == nodeId)"
                                @onclick="@CancelRename">
                            <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                        </button>
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="node-oval @(ssub.IsActive ? "" : "is-inactive")">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="circle" Class="node-icon" Style="color: var(--rz-warning); font-size: 0.625rem;" />
                        <span class="node-label">@ssub.Name</span>
                        <span class="node-actions">
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="action-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["EditButton"]"
                                    aria-label="@Loc["EditButton"]"
                                    disabled="@_isRenaming"
                                    @onclick="@(() => StartRenameSubSub(categoryId, subId, ssub))">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="edit" />
                            </button>
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="action-btn @(ssub.IsActive ? "action-toggle-will-deactivate" : "action-toggle-will-activate")"
                                    title="@(ssub.IsActive ? Loc["DeactivateButton"] : Loc["ActivateButton"])"
                                    aria-label="@(ssub.IsActive ? Loc["DeactivateButton"] : Loc["ActivateButton"])"
                                    disabled="@_isToggling"
                                    @onclick="@(() => HandleToggleSubSubActiveAsync(categoryId, subId, ssub))">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="@(ssub.IsActive ? "block" : "check_circle")" />
                            </button>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                }
            </div>
            @* Leaf node — no children, no end-of-group + button. *@
        </div>
    };
}

@* ── List-view render fragments ─────────────────────────────────────
   v6: These mirror the tree-view render fragments above (same data,
   same actions, same state) but produce the classic file-explorer
   layout: rows stacked vertically with indentation + elbow connectors
   showing parent-child relationships.

   They are COMPLETELY SEPARATE from the tree render fragments so the
   tree markup is untouched (per the user's instruction: "do not change
   the tree/node parts"). The list fragments reuse the same .action-btn,
   .chevron-btn, .group-add-btn CSS classes so the action buttons look
   consistent across both views. The list-specific layout (.list-row,
   .list-children, .list-node-label) is in the <style> block above. *@

@code {

    // ── List-view render: Category (depth 0) ──
    private RenderFragment RenderCategoryListItem(CategoryDto category) => __builder =>
    {
        var nodeId = "cat:" + category.Id.ToString();
        var isRenaming = _renamingNode == nodeId;
        var isAddingSub = _addingSubTo == category.Id;
        var isExpanded = _expandedCategories.Contains(category.Id) || isAddingSub;

        <div class="list-row @(category.IsActive ? "" : "is-inactive")">
            @if (isRenaming)
            {
                <input class="rename-input"
                       value="@_renameValue"
                       @oninput="@(e => _renameValue = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                       @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleRenameCategoryAsync(category.Id); })"
                       @ref="_renameInputRef" />
            }
            else
            {
                <button type="button"
                        class="chevron-btn @(isExpanded ? "is-expanded" : "")"
                        title="@(isExpanded ? Loc["Collapse"] : Loc["Expand"])"
                        aria-label="@(isExpanded ? Loc["Collapse"] : Loc["Expand"])"
                        aria-expanded="@isExpanded"
                        disabled="@_isRenaming"
                        @onclick="@(() => ToggleExpandCategory(category.Id))">
                    <RadzenIcon Icon="expand_more" />
                </button>
                <RadzenIcon Icon="folder" Class="node-icon" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                <span class="list-node-label">@category.Name</span>
            }
            <span class="row-actions">
                @if (isRenaming)
                {
                    <button type="button"
                            class="action-btn"
                            title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                            disabled="@(_isRenaming && _renamingNode == nodeId)"
                            @onclick="@(() => HandleRenameCategoryAsync(category.Id))">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                    </button>
                    <button type="button"
                            class="action-btn"
                            title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                            disabled="@(_isRenaming && _renamingNode == nodeId)"
                            @onclick="@CancelRename">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                    </button>
                }
                else
                {
                    <button type="button"
                            class="action-btn"
                            title="@Loc["EditButton"]"
                            aria-label="@Loc["EditButton"]"
                            disabled="@_isRenaming"
                            @onclick="@(() => StartRenameCategory(category))">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="edit" />
                    </button>
                    <button type="button"
                            class="action-btn @(category.IsActive ? "action-toggle-will-deactivate" : "action-toggle-will-activate")"
                            title="@(category.IsActive ? Loc["DeactivateButton"] : Loc["ActivateButton"])"
                            aria-label="@(category.IsActive ? Loc["DeactivateButton"] : Loc["ActivateButton"])"
                            disabled="@_isToggling"
                            @onclick="@(() => HandleToggleCategoryActiveAsync(category))">
                        <RadzenIcon Icon="@(category.IsActive ? "block" : "check_circle")" />
                    </button>
                }
            </span>
        </div>

        @if (isExpanded)
        {
            <div class="list-children">
                @foreach (var sub in category.SubCategories)
                {
                    @RenderSubListItem(category.Id, sub)
                }

                @* End-of-group + button for this Category's sub-cats. *@
                <div class="list-add-row">
                    @if (isAddingSub)
                    {
                        <div class="inline-add-form">
                            <input class="name-input"
                                   value="@_newSubName"
                                   @oninput="@(e => _newSubName = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "")"
                                   @onkeypress="@(async e => { if (e.Key == "Enter") await HandleCreateSubAsync(category.Id); })"
                                   @ref="_subInputRef" />
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="action-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["SaveButton"]"
                                    disabled="@(_isCreating && _creatingFor == $"sub:{category.Id}")"
                                    @onclick="@(() => HandleCreateSubAsync(category.Id))">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="check" />
                            </button>
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="action-btn"
                                    title="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                    disabled="@(_isCreating && _creatingFor == $"sub:{category.Id}")"
                                    @onclick="@CancelAddSub">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                            </button>
                        </div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <button type="button"
                                class="group-add-btn"
                                title="@Loc["AddSubCategoryButton"]"
                                aria-label="@Loc["AddSubCategoryButton"]"
                                disabled="@_isCreating"
                                @onclick="@(() => StartAddSub(category.Id))">
                            <span class="add-icon-circle">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="add" />
                            </span>
                            <span class="add-label">@Loc["AddSubCategoryButton"]</span>
                        </button>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        }
    };

    // ── List-view render: SubCategory (depth 1) ──
    private RenderFragment RenderSubListItem(Guid categoryId, SubCategoryDto sub) => __builder =>
    {
        var nodeId = "sub:" + sub.Id.ToString();
        var isRenaming = _renamingNode == nodeId;
        var isAddingSubSub = _addingSubSubTo == sub.Id;
        var isExpanded = _expandedSubs.Contains(sub.Id) || isAddingSubSub;

        <div class="list-row @(sub.IsActive ? "" : "is-inactive")">
            @if (isRenaming)
            {
                <input class="rename-input"
